    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (79.38) and **Kyle Tucker** (78.13). **Gunnar Henderson** remains the cornerstone of our lineup, bolstered by a dynamic platoon advantage against Michael McGreevy and his favorable #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** enters today with the highest SP skill bump of the day (+19%) as he squares off against the vulnerable arm of AJ Smith-Shawver. We also expect strong production from **Jackson Merrill** (75.26) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.96), both of whom benefit from pitching matchups where the opponent\u2019s xERA exceeds 4.75, providing a clear path to high-efficiency run and RBI generation.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision was leaving **Luis Robert Jr.** (46.94) on the bench. While his underlying skill set remains potent, his score was suppressed by a poor platoon dynamic against Dustin May and an \"Elite Hold\" label on the opposing starter that significantly dampens his stolen base potential. Consequently, the optimizer favored the higher current efficiency of **Dominic Smith** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Sam Antonacci** carries some risk due to a negative platoon split against MacKenzie Gore, his lead-off position provides the volume necessary to remain in the starting nine. We continue to monitor all lineups\u2014specifically for **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Nasim Nunez**\u2014as the \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces volatility; should any of these hitters drop significantly in their respective batting orders, their scores will likely contract, potentially forcing a shuffle to ensure we aren't burning game caps on suboptimal slots.",
